# carts/dialogue - walkthrough, second answer: the same reading, the OTHER branch
# ("Row to the shoal"), which finishes on the ending THE SHOAL LIGHT.
#
#     quarp replay record carts/dialogue -o /tmp/wa.qrpr --ticks 1500 \
#         --input-file carts/dialogue/replays/walkthrough-alt.input
#
# Identical to walkthrough.input except for one thing: a Down tap is dropped in between
# every pair of X taps. Down does nothing at all while a line is being read, and the
# choice menu clamps at its last option instead of wrapping, so a Down tap is a no-op
# everywhere except the one place it matters and repeating it costs nothing. That is why
# this file, like its twin, does not have to know on which tick the menu shows up - and
# why the pair of them proves the branch and not the timing.
#
# Timeline at 128x72: the tap on tick 740 opens the menu, the Down tap on tick 750 moves the
# cursor to the second option - the cartridge sees it on tick 751, and 751 is exactly the
# first tick on which the two tracks draw different pixels - the tap on tick 760 confirms
# it, and from tick 1061 the screen is THE SHOAL LIGHT and frozen. The two branches no
# longer finish on the same tick the way they did in the small font: both are eight windows
# long, but this one's last window carries a line more, and one more line is one more tap's
# worth of typing.
